{
  "dom_id": "step-31229",
  "name": "Example: \n                    Identifying a Quadratic Curve Type From Its Reduced Equation: No Cross-Product Term",
  "problem": "Which of the following equations define a non-empty set of points in the ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/multivariable/14235563/assets/e60bf9596889dbea2f6719078ad7817e12f96063cae887630abdd448e132437e.svg)-plane?\n\nI. ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/multivariable/14235563/assets/3da52050877a2855dba7355e4bbdd91e95ad7cd31fe62ff8d5d0c6ca895f6589.svg)\n\nII. ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/multivariable/14235563/assets/b0aa9bc434b0d9350630088f346e42243e24219ee4086b0b3563e6cc64bd552f.svg)\n\nIII. ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/multivariable/14235563/assets/17750e29fd96388982c719635201ad4788c2c6d40352b96d3daba019fce8db12.svg)",
  "worked_solution": "Let's examine each of the equations in turn.  \n\n- The equation ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/multivariable/14235563/assets/3da52050877a2855dba7355e4bbdd91e95ad7cd31fe62ff8d5d0c6ca895f6589.svg) defines a non-empty set. It represents the point   ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/multivariable/14235563/assets/11fcd48b1c7ad209409abaa1d91d8c374286782f2f426108d0ef29ee47602ad4.svg) in the ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/multivariable/14235563/assets/e15fa72f0cdfc4bb75a38b1aa53e99baad6ed04b742e19b31d9c80f809bbd26e.svg)-plane.\n\n- The equation ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/multivariable/14235563/assets/b0aa9bc434b0d9350630088f346e42243e24219ee4086b0b3563e6cc64bd552f.svg) defines an empty set. Notice that the left-hand side is non-negative for all ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/multivariable/14235563/assets/8c33e6564649c3beca9591e67622629ffab451061b8a92931451ef854d188bcd.svg) and ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/multivariable/14235563/assets/f0b10bbcfd13006bc3490f782396e26677fa5c329dd8a770c828aa9ca9011eb3.svg) while the right-hand side is negative.\n\n- The equation ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/multivariable/14235563/assets/17750e29fd96388982c719635201ad4788c2c6d40352b96d3daba019fce8db12.svg) defines a non-empty set. It represents a  pair of intersecting lines, ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/multivariable/14235563/assets/012aab369190f18204bc3b4530eb5fd7eed60908a2fa25a7cfd3dac1f9d76402.svg) and ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/multivariable/14235563/assets/eefefdeef49074edb3f06e7072ba2fc144ade0c05c90510b72b0c8d4eb0871ed.svg)\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I  and III only.\"",
